+First height probes. For new-height round1 apply the same empirical argmin to previous-height round1 samples individually scaled by |R|_now/|R|_then and rounded up. The scaled samples use the same upper-median censor ordering; they do not authorize returning to probe mode once a prefix exists. Previous |R|=0 or absent usable history permits a probe only when this epoch has no prior prefix. Record end-round1 |R| and r=median estimatedRoundStartDifference/|R| as a diagnostic; the sample-by-sample scaling, not a single median substitution, controls request sizing. Reorg/disconnect height transition uses available saved round1 information, otherwise probes.
