+The frozen sizing table is a reproducible empirical distribution table independent of M. d=0 gives prefix length1 for every quantile. For positive d generate2000 trials of d distinct uniform nonzero IDs, equiprobable signs, independent reference peeler. Grid={0..64} union {round(64*(11/10)^k)} through MAXIMUM_TABLE_DIFFERENCE=4096, including deduplicated endpoint4096; use nearest-integer half-up grid rounding. SplitMix64 seed0x534E4F5753544F52 supplies successive ID outputs, rejecting zero/duplicates; accepted ID's sign is the low bit of the next output. Generator cap=floor((2MiB−100)/28)=74894; cap-exhausted trials count as that cap.
