+The host owns callback completion/cancellation, not a hidden core timeout. Disconnect cancels the donor's in-flight token before payload interpretation and immediately retries an already known usable alternate. Cancelled results are stale before validation. Disconnect does not cancel awaitingAdmission: the body was already admitted by the host and its matching callback remains required unless tip cancels the generation.
