+
+Discover donors on algebraically consistent positive decode and successful one-shot reconstruction irrespective of exclusions; in particular every Pending ID in peerCandidates establishes that responder as an alternate. Keep at most min(D,8) usable donors per ID, ordered by first discovery then PeerID. Remove failed/disconnected/stale-generation candidates immediately, retaining separate unavailable marks. Failed sources cannot occupy all donor slots and block a later honest peer. Full usable slots preserve their ordered candidates; a subsequent failure frees a slot. Retry known alternatives immediately. One in-flight OR awaiting record per ID; host timeout returns notFound, while admitted callback completion remains the host obligation. Matching admission preserves the live item lifetime and applies the §8 entry gate; whole Pending state is preserved without changing preference or FINAL. Fresh ordinary admission initializes preference in, both success counters and evidence sum zero, and not FINAL. Preference/counters alone do not cancel fetches or create epoch rejection marks. All-unavailable leaves no Pending; probation persists to tip reset.
