+## §8 EVIDENCE-WEIGHTED ITEM ROUNDS AND ROOT SETTLEMENT
+
+D is the compatible connected peer population captured at round start. At small D, sample all D peers. The population at which K first drops below D is OPEN for the (f,K) grid; no crossover or replacement K formula is selected here. Experiments declare K explicitly, with 1<=K<=D. Select distinct peers uniformly from the canonical connected list using the seeded RNG. D=0 opens no round. maximumAdversaryFraction remains the host's adversary-fraction assumption, not the new per-item success threshold.
+
+Each nonfinal captured item receives at most one eligible observation per selected peer. Capture advertised raw A with incarnation/candidate bits and live Pending identities at round start, at most M+P records; post-capture items get no votes. Matching Pending admission preserves its lifetime and whole state; removal/readmission or loss of support invalidates prior-lifetime observations. Inbound polls never vote. FINAL items need no further votes.
+
+Votes express the responder's candidate preference. MATCH gives yes for captured W and no for other captured eligible IDs. At arrival, decoded-present and nonexcluded gives yes; decoded-absent or excluded gives no. An incomplete arrival gives no other sharing inference: remaining captured items abstain. A complete arrival classifies other eligible captured reference items as shared unless excluded. DIFF reconstructs the peer's advertised raw set from captured raw A, then applies exclusions; captured Pending absent from that assertion is absent. No takes precedence over presence. Rescue-only discoveries abstain that round, including a later complete rescue. Silent, late, invalid or discarded contradictory replies abstain.
+
+A node never casts a yes for its own Pending item: Pending is absent from its W, root, proof, advertised cells, setSize and exclusions. This does not prohibit receiving a yes from another node that has admitted the item. Such received votes score the poller's captured Pending lifetime and permit the expressly required FINAL-in Pending state. MATCH votes remain as before.
+
+For item x, voteCount=yesVoteCount+noVoteCount is the number of sampled peers casting valid votes on x. Set answerFloor=floor(K/2)+1. A round counts for x only if voteCount>=answerFloor; below this floor add0, count no success and change no item evidence/counters. For a counting round side s succeeds when sideVoteCount>=ceil(4*voteCount/5), where sideVoteCount is its actual vote count. The success denominator is voteCount, with the additional majority-of-K answer floor. This includes voteCount=0 as no success. For voteCount>0, at most one side can succeed. A no-success round adds zero and resets nothing.
+
